Bound native recursion in WebAssembly, where the stack pointer cannot see it.

JavaScriptCore guards recursion by comparing the stack pointer with a limit,
but in WebAssembly most of a native frame lives on the engine's own stack,
out of the stack pointer's sight: deep native recursion (proxy traps that
recurse, recursive getters, deeply nested JSON) overflowed the engine and
killed it instead of throwing a RangeError. Nested interpreter entries are
now counted and limited, which makes such recursion fail with a catchable
RangeError, and the fast JSON stringifier hands deep nesting to the general
one, which does not recurse natively.

